The tokens, the Default skin, the colour modes, headings and block styles moved to `content.css`, so the editor shows the content like the Public UI; `publicui.css` styles the frame in the `custom` layer, and nothing is unlayered. The brand color is `--brand`, and `--accent` is a subtle hover fill again. `@plone/layout` lays out the stack of blocks and applies the gutter and the room around the content. The title and the navigation align separately (`--align`, `--nav-align`): Default has a left aligned title and a centred navigation. A centred navigation is centred on the page, and the breadcrumbs' home icon sits on the text's centre line. Logging in and out are pills: logging in the primary action, logging out the secondary. In the Default skin, the quote is glass with the page's gradient, the callout has a tint of the gradient's bloom colour (`--callout-background`), and teasers are glass cards, as in the first prototype. Sizes come from token scales: a spacing scale from `--space`, a type scale from `--font-size`, and line height, radius, tracking, control and icon size tokens, with every value rounded to a step. Responsive rules are container queries on the header, footer and content containers, and a centred navigation is a style query on `--nav-align`, which replaces the `--header-columns` token. The bundled Funnel fonts declare their weight range and an italic face. Only the Default skin is active; Nieve stays in `content.css`, commented out, as an example of another skin. The page is light whatever the OS prefers: the colour tokens carry their dark values, and `data-mode="dark"` on `<html>` switches the Public UI to them, while the editor's content stays light. The header scrolls with the page; `data-sticky="on"` on `<html>` makes it sticky, and nothing sets it yet. Full width blocks keep the page gutter (`--full-width-gutter: keep`, a style query); a skin can let them run to the edges. Teasers lift on hover by `--card-lift`, 2px. Headings follow one ramp: each level from h6 (the body size) up is one half step of `--type-scale` above the next, h5 and h6 take the skin's heading style, and the room above a heading is 1.5 times its size. @danalvrz
